WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.570
I'm going to blame everything on him until he

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.620
learns how to talk.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.840
You gotta make U-ey.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.290
I don't know how to do that.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.320
Stop this car!

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.990
Haley, honey, did you mean to send this text

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.160
to your dad? Text.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.330
What does it say?

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.020
Um.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.110
I hate to spoil your golf game, but.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.600
Yeah I know, no, I didn't send that.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.490
Must have accidentally dictated when you and

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.600
dad were talking.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.930
Okay. That's weird.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.600
Well, while I have you on the phone, would

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.670
you mind emptying the dishwasher and- You're

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.740
breaking up? Haley, can you hear me now?

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.810
Nope. Bye. Got it.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.870
Told you we'd get it.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.840
Now, just for a little creative editing.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.320
Your mind is so brilliant.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.610
If you put this much effort into your

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.440
schoolwork, there is no telling the things-

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.030
Why do you have to ruin everything?

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.500
I know she's always talking about my

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.520
potential.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:52.910
Fore!

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.280
Do you think I hit her?

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.300
Eh, She's fine.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.780
I'm sorry I'm so distracted today.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:00.680
What's wrong buddy?

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.650
Let me ask you something.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.450
Do you ever get the sense that your wife

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.830
feels like she could have done better?

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.490
God, no.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.380
No. She's the luckiest woman on earth.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.580
I mean, if anything, I could have done

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.080
better. The noises that come out of that

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.240
woman at night, it's like she's that black

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.530
guy from police academy.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.820
Oh, speak of the devil.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.440
Message for my wife. Not the black guy from

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.690
police academy. Oh, that'd be so awesome.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.530
That'd be neat.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.500
Hey, it's Claire. I hate to spoil your golf

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.270
game, but I'm pregnant.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.250
What? Let's talk as soon as you can.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:30.650
I have to leave.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.360
What? We're in the middle of a game.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.560
I have to be with Claire.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.830
Okay. We've been going over your story.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.000
And it doesn't add up.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.440
My purse was too high for you to reach.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.620
He's tall enough to reach up here.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.080
He knocked over the baby powder trying to

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.060
get my stuffed animals.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.950
I'm not buying it. Look, you can see the

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.570
footprints where you walked.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:51.470
Walk?

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.550
Lily! Lily!

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.210
Lily!

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.780
Joe can't walk.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.180
He does for me.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.750
So you have ways of making him walk?

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.940
Lily, just admit that you did it.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:03.310
Come here, Joe.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:06.610
Like you did before.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:07.800
You're embarrassing yourself.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.000
Hey Joe. He can't walk.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.470
He's walking.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:16.690
The candles that I leaved work.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.830
Look at the stride on him.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.900
He's as sure footed as a mountain goat.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:20.950
Told you.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.950
I'm so sorry that we doubted you.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.990
Boy, did I get lucky.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.010
I'm going to blame everything on him until

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.330
he learns how to talk.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.920
If I don't make it to Canada, your mom wins,

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.390
and this baby ends up in the garage first

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.350
thing in the morning.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.240
Our garage? I'm in charge of the recycling.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.660
I'm supposed to bring it from the garage to

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.730
the curb by 6 a.m. Thursday morning.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.440
I may have missed a few weeks.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:56.690
Shoot. Maybe more than a few weeks.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.570
After a while, the pile just got so big I

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.070
couldn't bring out the night before or eople

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.300
would ask questions.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.790
I don't need people asking questions.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:05.910
Then you're right. You've got to finish.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.300
You'll never use this thing in the garage.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.620
It's too drafty. That's why I'm.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.880
Going to Canada, buddy.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.080
To avoid the draft.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.110
Okay. Your turn.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.520
Oh. No way.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.440
Do you want to get her attention or not?

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.810
That was amazing

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.690
Did you see the look on Miranda's face?

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.300
No, but you did good, Thelma.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.500
Please stop calling me that.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.640
I hate that movie.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:44.780
What movie?

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.420
Uh oh. Dead end.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:48.920
You gotta make a u-ey.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.360
I don't know how to do that.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.560
Mind moving your thumb?

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.460
Alexandra.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.040
That's what that's short for?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.420
So sweet of you to take them to the park.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.060
Just make sure there's someplace shady.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:21.910
We'll do.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.160
Fridgerator. No.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.770
Say frigerator.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.660
Refrigerator. I need you to focus, kid.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.740
Fridgorfrator?

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.450
Where we keep the sandwiches.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.100
People seem delighted by Joe.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.410
Whatever. But I had that fetching study

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:37.600
partner coming over, and I realized I could

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.280
use Joe's by the numbers cuteness to my

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.540
amorous advantage.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.900
Wow. Even for me, that was a lot of Manny.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.800
But a sandwich.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.180
It's like you're not even trying.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.560
Okay. That's probably her.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.980
Look, just be cute, okay?

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.340
For my sake. It's like when guys use puppies

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.390
to attract girls.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.720
Hi, Manny. Olive, please come in.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.670
That's my little brother, Joe.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.290
Don't mind his little pot there.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.450
What do you have in there again?

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:03.810
Some kind of pasta dish.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.690
Woof, woof. Oh, are you a doggy?

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.790
Yeah. He's always doing adorable stuff like

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:09.960
that because I'm his hero.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:10.830
I love that.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.980
Are you a good doggy or a bad doggy?

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:14.820
Grr.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.800
Oh, scary.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.900
Adorable. I know.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.100
So, should we head up?

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.980
Oh! Oh, my God, get it off me!

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.240
No! Joe!

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.650
Joe! Joe! Let go!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.210
What are you doing? He's biting me!

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.580
Do something! No!

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:30.850
Bad joe. Bad joo!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.520
Oh, that's making him bite me harder.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.530
A person is not a sandwich, Joe!

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.000
Joe, what are you doing?

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.110
Joe! Let go!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.610
We're leaving. See?

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.090
That idn't take too long.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.310
Thank you, girls.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.350
Now go and have a good time.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.380
All right. Bye.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.440
See, you don't need all the conflict.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.320
Note to Claire if you want intense family

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.450
drama, rent Spy Kids.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:52.930
They saved their parents lives.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:53.880
Do you think they would have done that if

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.350
they got yelled at all the time?

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.120
Sweet and sour chicken.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.330
Girls! Get back!

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.130
Gotta fix that step.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.210
Girls. Did he just yell?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:18.660
Drive!

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.710
I'm trying!

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.640
You girls get back here right now!

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:28.880
Pretend you don't hear him! Stop this car!

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.040
We're sorry, dad, we couldn't hear.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:32.850
No more lies!

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.290
You poked the bear.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.480
Girls, you poked him!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.050
We bribed

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.700
Lily with all the soda she could drink.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.980
And threw a party. It was going great until

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:42.750
someone set off the alarm because he just

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.440
had to smoke his dorky pipe.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.980
Dorky? Yeah, because Hugh Hefner doesn't get

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.870
girls. I love you too, mommy.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.670
All clear party people.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.810
I told her we were baking cookies.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.460
Dude, our oven's broken.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.350
My mom's definitely gonna get suspicious and

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.370
check on us. That means my

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.540
Mom's coming, too.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.070
I'll get everyone to leave. You get rid of

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.720
the beer and your idea of a spread.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.420
Wait, we're not giving up yet.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.460
The beer pong tournament just started.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.440
The girls are laughing at all of our jokes,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.540
and they think we're friends with guys like

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:16.260
Tommy Cudahy.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.030
Great party. Lewis.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:19.530
Thanks, Tommy.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:20.970
From now on, I'm Lewis.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.670
We're going to get caught if we do nothing.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.390
What if we hide everyone long enough for my

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:26.010
mom to check on us and then leave?

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.000
It's not worth it.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.540
Guys, when do we play?

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.020
Seven hours in Heaven.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.930
Moving the party upstairs, people.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.200
Knock, knock. Yeah.

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.480
Hi, Miss Pasternak.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.640
I got to go meet some friends.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.200
I'll see you guys later, okay? Be careful.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:40.950
Here.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.870
I brought by some more liquor bottles for

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:43.920
Lily's project.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.880
What project?

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:47.520
I don't know, I caught her going through my

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.410
garbage and she said she needed liquor

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.740
bottles. That's weird.

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:52.630
Anyway, tell her I'll have a couple more for

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:53.190
her tomorrow.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.360
Okay. Bye bye.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.370
Take care. She can't babysit anymore.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.230
What project? I don't know.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.670
We've got a problem here.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.920
Look what I found under Dwight's bed.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:03.720
Oh, yeah.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.850
It's too bad he brought such a great energy

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:06.840
to the house.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.640
Mitchell. I just need a minute to process

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:09.090
this.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.650
Last weekend, Mom and dad went to the

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.030
Artichoke Festival in Monterey.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.410
And Dylan's mom had the twins.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.270
So we took the opportunity to have a little

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.490
party just to see if we still had it in us.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:18.450
We did.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.430
I'm checking the pizza.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.440
Got a pizza guy. Got a pizza guy.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.240
His name is Abraham.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.750
Don't forget the garlic knots.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.240
Garlic knots. Garlic knots.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:27.930
Yo.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.440
This party is the goat.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.580
Greatest of all time. I'm Doug, I'm across

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.050
the street. Neighbor was just curbing my

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:34.350
bins.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.390
Heard the party noise. Thought I'd join up.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.680
Want a refill on that?

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.990
There is no scenario where I accept a drink

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.280
from you. Lit.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:44.520
Nice to see the Dunphy

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.030
Name still

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:46.200
Carries some party clout.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.650
Oh, you know, we're running low on jungle

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.600
juice. Just soak it up with a towel and

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:55.120
wring it back into the cup. Okay.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.030
Cool. What kind is that?

00:08:57.660 --> 00:08:59.640
Can I have one conversation tonight without

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.590
someone asking me about my snake?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.830
Oh, good Lord, what happened?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.390
I slipped on that drink you spilled.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.660
Oh, hurt my ankle really bad.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.580
I mean, I don't want to sue you, but I don't

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.990
really see any other option.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:13.890
Do you?

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.420
So now I work for Doug.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:18.860
Hey, everybody.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:20.650
Abraham.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.270
Don't stare at it. Put it out.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.380
We made some temporary fixes and scheduled

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.330
repairs for today when Mom and Dad said

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.570
they'd be at the beach.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.150
Then they came home early.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.040
It's just hard when you can't trust family

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:38.970
members.

